{"parentUuid":"450bfecd-7a43-42b8-96c0-7278fdf4c1f2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZvWBuXgaNPVYev3b5zm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QkogkaonDW8nKdQiiGy7TQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && S=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad && make test 2>&1 | tail -1 && ls eval/gold/ && git add eval/gold/POLICY.md && git diff --cached > $S/staged-x.diff && uv run python $S/scan_staged.py .env $S/staged-x.diff; echo \"host matches: $(grep -c -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\" $S/staged-x.diff)\"; git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nPOLICY.md version 2 (2026-10-31), after the draw and before any label\n\nThe EM's amendments, in one dated commit:\n- rule 19, spirit-adjacent claims: dreams and visions of the dead, omens and death\n  warnings, poltergeists, clairvoyance with no spirit, and spirit photographs, with\n  judged examples where they exist, each checked to be outside gold and dev\n- the signals where rules 6 and 9 meet, for fact against tale\n- rule 16: where several merged items are reports, the fields come from the one\n  holding the lexicon's match, else the first\n- place_type in the schema's values (inn_or_hotel and the rest)\n- the label record's slices, E1 to E14 but E9, which comes from the grouping\n\nThe split keeps recording version 1's sha256, the policy it was drawn under. Git order\nis version 1, the draw, version 2, then the labels, so RDR-3 still holds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit push -q origin phase-2c-reader 2>&1 | grep -v -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\"; git log --oneline -1; git ls-remote origin refs/heads/phase-2c-reader","description":"Commit POLICY v2 alone, push, and verify"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence